# Mind Tools: Mathematics as Cognitive Extension

A *mind tool* is a formal system that extends what a thinking agent can directly apprehend. We model a formal system by the set of statements it can prove, and we say one system is at least as powerful as another when it proves everything the other does. This notebook lets you explore the whole theory hands-on.

## 1. What makes something a mind tool?

A system $F$ is a mind tool relative to a brain $B$ exactly when $B \prec F$ — when $F$ proves *strictly more* than $B$. Try building your own systems and comparing them:

